  "glossaryRoiTerm": "ROI (Return on Investment)",
  "glossaryRoiDef": "Measures how much you recover for every dollar invested in a crop. It is calculated as (Income − Expenses) ÷ Expenses. A negative ROI means the crop spends more than it recovers: for example, an ROI of −70% means that for every $100 invested only $30 come back.",
  "glossaryBalanceTerm": "Balance / Result",
  "glossaryBalanceDef": "Income minus Expenses in a period. If the result is positive you have a gain; if negative, a loss.",
  "glossaryMarginTerm": "Margin on sales",
  "glossaryMarginDef": "Of every $100 you sell, how much remains as profit after covering expenses. A margin of 20% means that for every $100 sold, $20 remain.",
  "glossaryRatioTerm": "Expenses vs income",
  "glossaryRatioDef": "What percentage of your income goes to expenses. For example, 80% means that for every $100 that come in, $80 are spent and $20 remain.",
  "glossaryAvgTerm": "Monthly historical average",
  "glossaryAvgDef": "The average of what you spend per month in a category (for example, labor). It serves as a reference to detect unusual increases in your expenses.",
